               "x"
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "\\( 3^{x} \\) is an exponential function with a constant base, so its derivative is \\( 3^{x} \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} \\); the power rule does not apply to it.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            [
               "Power",
               3,
               "x"
            ],
            [
               "Ln",
               3
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The factor \\( \\left(1 + \\sin(2x)\\right)^{3} \\) is a cube of \\( 1 + \\sin(2x) \\), which contains a sine of \\( 2x \\), so apply the chain rule from the outside inward: \\( \\left(\\left(1 + \\sin(2x)\\right)^{3}\\right)' = 6 \\left(\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 1\\right)^{2} \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} \\).",
